WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.936
[MUSIC PLAYING]

00:00:06.900 --> 00:00:09.480
SPEAKER: If you haven't done
so already, set up your project

00:00:09.480 --> 00:00:12.450
and create a Google
Cloud Storage bucket.

00:00:12.450 --> 00:00:15.450
In the Cloud Console, on
the Project Selector page,

00:00:15.450 --> 00:00:18.850
select or create
a Cloud project.

00:00:18.850 --> 00:00:21.450
Make sure that billing is
enabled for your Google Cloud

00:00:21.450 --> 00:00:22.530
project.

00:00:22.530 --> 00:00:25.080
Learn how to confirm billing
is enabled for your project

00:00:25.080 --> 00:00:26.660
in the links below.

00:00:26.660 --> 00:00:28.620
Enable the Cloud Vision API.

00:00:40.040 --> 00:00:44.210
Now create a Cloud Storage
bucket in the Cloud Console.

00:00:44.210 --> 00:00:46.390
Go to the Cloud
Storage browser page.

00:00:46.390 --> 00:00:49.060
Click Create Bucket.

00:00:49.060 --> 00:00:51.820
Assign a unique bucket name.

00:00:51.820 --> 00:00:54.430
Do not include sensitive
information in the bucket name,

00:00:54.430 --> 00:00:58.730
because the bucket namespace
is global and publicly visible.

00:00:58.730 --> 00:01:02.150
Select the location where the
bucket data will be stored.

00:01:02.150 --> 00:01:04.940
For default storage
class, select Standard.

00:01:04.940 --> 00:01:07.490
Then, click Create.

00:01:07.490 --> 00:01:10.610
Now you can make requests
via the Vision API.

00:01:10.610 --> 00:01:14.880
Download this demo
image linked below.

00:01:14.880 --> 00:01:17.280
Open the Cloud Console
storage browser.

00:01:17.280 --> 00:01:19.400
Select the bucket
you just created.

00:01:19.400 --> 00:01:23.390
Click Upload Files, and select
the demo image JPEG file

00:01:23.390 --> 00:01:25.430
to upload from
your local machine

00:01:25.430 --> 00:01:27.440
to your Cloud Storage bucket.

00:01:27.440 --> 00:01:29.180
After the file is
uploaded and listed

00:01:29.180 --> 00:01:31.805
in the Cloud Storage browser,
share the image publicly.

00:01:43.330 --> 00:01:46.120
Open the interactive API
Explorer template found

00:01:46.120 --> 00:01:47.950
in the guide linked below.

00:01:47.950 --> 00:01:49.450
Complete the
template by replacing

00:01:49.450 --> 00:01:53.410
cloud-samples-data/vision in the
image dot source dot imageUri

00:01:53.410 --> 00:01:56.320
field with the name of the
Cloud Storage bucket where you

00:01:56.320 --> 00:01:59.320
uploaded the demo
image dot JPEG file.

00:01:59.320 --> 00:02:01.705
Click Execute to send the
request to the service.

00:02:05.420 --> 00:02:08.220
The JSON response appears here.

00:02:08.220 --> 00:02:09.479
Congratulations.

00:02:09.479 --> 00:02:12.180
You've just made your first
images annotate request

00:02:12.180 --> 00:02:14.250
to the Cloud Vision API service.

00:02:14.250 --> 00:02:16.480
To learn more about
specific features,

00:02:16.480 --> 00:02:19.110
see example annotations,
and get annotations

00:02:19.110 --> 00:02:21.540
for an individual file
or image, check out

00:02:21.540 --> 00:02:23.130
the Cloud documentation.

00:02:23.130 --> 00:02:26.180
[MUSIC PLAYING]

